# Allowlist style: ignore everything, then un-ignore only the config worth publishing.
#
# Rationale: this repo is a PUBLIC, hand-maintained copy of ~/.claude. It is not a
# remote of that directory — files get copied across manually, so a stray `cp -R` can
# carry over session transcripts, job-search notes, or every typed prompt (projects/,
# jobs/, file-history/, history.jsonl, settings.local.json). Once pushed to a repo
# other people have cloned, deleting it does not unpublish it.
#
# A blocklist that ever misses one of those leaks PII permanently. This inverts the
# risk: new files and directories are ignored by default, and only the paths below
# can ever be tracked. Adding something new to the repo must be a deliberate edit here.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/settings.json
!/CLAUDE.md
!/statusline.sh
!/hooks/
!/commands/
!/skills/

# Re-ignore backup/cruft even inside the allowlisted dirs above (last match wins).
# The PreToolUse hook drops *.bak next to any Write-tool edit; those are not restore points.
*.bak
.DS_Store
